---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { GOSPEL_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE, STUDIO_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`The Gospel | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description={GOSPEL_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="gospel-page">
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<SiteHeader />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
			<header class="gospel-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">The Gospel</p>
				<h1>Good news for a weary world.</h1>
				<p class="gospel-intro__lead">
					The message of the gospel is that God loves people deeply, humanity is broken by sin,
					and Jesus Christ came to bring forgiveness, reconciliation, and new life.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="gospel-section" aria-labelledby="gospel-need-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">God and humanity</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-need-title">God created us for relationship with Him.</h2>
					<p>
						God is the holy, righteous Creator of all things. He made humanity in His own image,
						with dignity, purpose, and the capacity to know Him and love Him (Genesis 1:26-27; Psalm
						8:4-9). But Adam and Eve rebelled against God, and all humanity fell under sin. We all
						share in that broken condition, and the consequences are real: broken relationships, shame,
						confusion, and spiritual death (Romans 3:23; Isaiah 59:2).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section gospel-section--light" aria-labelledby="gospel-christ-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">The answer</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-christ-title">God sent Jesus Christ.</h2>
					<p>
						Jesus Christ is the Son of God, the Savior of sinners, and the one who perfectly
						revealed God's love (John 1:1-14; Hebrews 4:15). He lived a sinless life, died on the
						cross to bear the judgment that our sin deserved, and rose bodily from the grave in
						victory over sin and death (1 Corinthians 15:3-4). The cross is not merely a symbol of
						morality or kindness; it is the decisive act by which God made a way for us to be
						forgiven and restored.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section" aria-labelledby="gospel-grace-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Grace</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-grace-title">Salvation is God's gift, received by faith.</h2>
					<p>
						Salvation is not earned by good works, moral effort, religious performance, or the
						strength of our own will (Ephesians 2:8-9). It is the free gift of God's grace, offered
						to us through Jesus Christ. Repentance means turning away from sin and trusting Jesus;
						faith means receiving him as Lord and Savior (Acts 3:19; Romans 10:9-10). This is not a
						magical formula or a self-help plan. It is a humble surrender to the one who alone can
						save.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section gospel-section--light" aria-labelledby="gospel-response-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Response</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-response-title">Repent and believe.</h2>
					<p>
						The gospel calls us to repent of sin and trust in Jesus Christ (Mark 1:15; Acts 2:38).
						This is not a demand for perfection before God welcomes us. It is an invitation to receive
						the forgiveness that God offers, to put our trust in Christ, and to begin a life of
						discipleship. Following Jesus means learning from Scripture, prayer, and the life of the
						church, while growing in obedience, love, and humility (2 Timothy 3:16-17; Hebrews 10:24-25).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-callout" aria-labelledby="gospel-questions-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Questions or next steps</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-questions-title">We would be glad to talk with you.</h2>
					<p>
						If you have questions about the Christian faith, want to know more about following
						Jesus, or are seeking a conversation, send us a note at
						<a href={`mailto:${STUDIO_EMAIL}`}>{STUDIO_EMAIL}</a> or use the contact form below.
						We are not offering pastoral counseling or a replacement for a local church, but we
						are glad to speak with people who are seeking to understand the gospel.
					</p>
					<div class="gospel-callout__actions">
						<a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Ask a question</a>
						<a class="button button--quiet" href={`mailto:${STUDIO_EMAIL}?subject=Question%20about%20the%20gospel`}>
							Email Petalwake <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>
